Patch 7933 (diagnostic): GPU_TIME=1 names where the GPU time goes.

The [GPUT] line (patch 2906, every 120 batches) now gives ms per batch, draws per batch and how busy the GPU was over the wall time of
those batches (near 100 %: GPU-bound; low: the GPU waits for the CPU), then the ten costliest passes by name: rt:<offset> WxH,
depth:<offset> WxH (depth-only), display WxH, start(uploads,copies) (texture uploads and copies before the first target switch),
post(composite,AA,HUD,present), vram-copy (VPULL_VRAM, patch 7934), each with ms per batch, how many times it ran and its draws.
The last query slot is kept for the end mark, so a batch with more than 1023 target switches still measures its whole span
("marks dropped" says so; the last recorded pass keeps counting the draws after it). Off (GPU_TIME unset): nothing is recorded, as before.

